Or a wand/potion of enlightenment. (Which is not always handy either.)

The way I see it, prayer is quite literally for situations where only
divine intervention can save your bacon. The fact that prayers are cut
off in Gehennom is a good marker of the utility of prayer: by that
point in the game, you should be able to handle things on your own.
Before that point, yes, you're likely to need some extra help. On your
way back up, you may need a little divine nudge once, or at most
twice. From my experience and observations, the number of turns
between leaving Gehennom for the last time and the final altar isn't a
whole lot greater than the usual prayer timeout for someone with the
demigod flag set for killing Rodney, and is definitely less than that
for someone who's both demigod and crowned. (If you're ninja enough to
obtain the Amulet without killing Rodney, you don't need no steenkin'
divine help!) If you need more help than that from your god at that
stage of the game, then maybe you're not meant to ascend anyhow, and
the mechanism of calculating prayer timeout reflects that. (In the
context of the game's mythology, of course. This isn't meant to be a
comment on playing ability.)

The crapshoot is that the situation where prayer is most helpful --
the divine full heal -- is under circumstances that would likely prove
fatal if you're wrong about the state of your prayer timeout. Can you
afford to be immobilized without invulnerability for three turns with
less than 1/7 of your maxHP to your name? Once you're on your way to
Astral, the only time this is likely is if you're actively being
beaten upon, and so the answer is usually "no". But again...if you
need significant help from your god at that stage (or indeed need to
call for help very often at any stage), then maybe you're not so
Chosen after all.


